  "remaining_fields": {
    "second_threshold": [
      "E802 type3 attr3B handler 738B88 puts zero in first payload word and caller value in second, then invokes 738200. The second nonzero input uses the same LPWR+1318 multiplication and divide-by-1000 scale as the first. A801 3B returns the same provider second word scaled by floor(raw*1000/factor); 20801706 selector 2 returns the raw second word. This establishes shared numerical units with the first input under the same factor, not the distinct functional meaning.",
      "The ordinary 737120 controller0 default path selects parent+37C for its first word but hardcodes 1000000 as second input before the same scale; special GPU-property branches bypass the ordinary path and include alternate constants. The local threshold raw observation is consistent with this ordinary default but does not prove that branch ran.",
      "NVIDIA gk20a source calls a register pwr_pmu_pg_ppuidlefilth and programs it using named PMU_PG_POST_POWERUP_IDLE_THRESHOLD=1000000 (hw_pwr_gk20a.h:721, pmu_gk20a.h:974, pmu_gk20a.c:2317). That older GPU uses 0x10A6E8+4*i, whereas pinned Blackwell provider reads 0x8F7180+4*hardware-ID. Equal default value and adjacent first/second layout are suggestive, but no register lineage or firmware ABI establishes equivalence. Do not label attr3B post-powerup from this alone.",
      "No selected source path supplies a name or actual consumer for the current second word beyond firmware request 02/03/04 and the raw provider. A matched GB register definition or the current matching firmware receiver and its consumption semantics is the concrete missing join. A write/readback trial can establish a transition and peer preservation, not that missing meaning; no second-control trial is proposed on present evidence."
    ],
    "second_field_source_windows": [
      {
        "name": "ordinary_default_and_special_cases",
